    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0616" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 362.112T41/3</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram April 1, Thrasher case.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d511-f1"/> Endeavor if
                    possible to obtain from survivors of steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Falaba</hi> details regarding sinking of vessel by German submarine,
                    including any attempts at resistance by the <hi rendition="#italic">Falaba</hi>,
                    time given for crew and passengers to leave vessel, letter and number of
                    submarine, definite evidence showing that Thrasher was on board, and details as
                    to his drowning. Report briefly by cable as soon as possible. Urgent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
